# Dirijor + BMAD

## Product source of truth

- PRD: `docs/DIRIJOR-PRD.md`
- System diagram: `docs/architecture.mermaid`
- Project conventions / stack summary: `docs/project-context.md`

## BMAD in this repo

- Installed under `_bmad/` (BMM module) and configured for Cursor in `.cursor/skills/`. Config: `_bmad/_memory/config.yaml` (e.g. `output_folder: _bmad-output`).
- Before acting as a BMAD persona (architect, PM, analyst, etc.) or running a BMAD task, read the matching `SKILL.md` under `.cursor/skills/bmad-*/` and follow its activation/workflow instructions.
- BMAD CLI status/update command: `npx bmad-method status` or `npx bmad-method install --directory . --action update --modules bmm --tools cursor --yes`.
- Write BMAD workflow outputs under `_bmad-output/` (gitignored), not scattered in `docs/` unless the user asks to promote a specific artifact.

## Implementation discipline

- Keep PRD claims and architecture diagram aligned with what is actually implemented; call out stubs (e.g. supervisor consensus placeholder) when planning work.

## Git and story traceability

- Prefer **one story per commit** (or a clearly scoped series). Commit subjects should include the **BMAD story key** or an unambiguous scope; do not describe only one feature if the diff spans multiple story trees (see `docs/guides/git-and-story-commits.md`).
- After `git add`, run **`scripts/git/story-commit-hints.sh --staged`**; keep **`sprint-status.yaml`** `development_status` and the detailed **`stories:`** block in sync when you update statuses.
- Load **`.cursor/skills/bmad-story-git-traceability/SKILL.md`** when the user asks for commit/story alignment or “avoid megacommit / misaligned log.”
